Q: Not able to configure properly for @DateTimeFormat Spring 3
A: <p>You need to have a custom converter to convert from String to java.util.Date .
In your application context you probably have something like this:</p>

<pre><code>&lt;bean id="customEditorsRegistrar" class="org.springframework.batch.support.DefaultPropertyEditorRegistrar"&gt;
    &lt;property name="customEditors" ref="customEditors" /&gt;
&lt;/bean&gt;
</code></pre>

<p>If you do, you need to create and add a custom editor to the HashMap to have a converter from String to java.util.Date :</p>

<pre><code>&lt;bean id="customEditors" class="java.util.HashMap"&gt;
    &lt;constructor-arg&gt;
        &lt;map&gt;
            &lt;entry key="java.util.Date"&gt;
                &lt;bean class="org.springframework.beans.propertyeditors.CustomDateEditor"&gt;
                    &lt;constructor-arg&gt;
                        &lt;bean class="pt.xx.xxxx.xxxx.core.common.support.file.converter.UtilDateFormat" /&gt;
                    &lt;/constructor-arg&gt;
                    &lt;constructor-arg value="true" /&gt;
                &lt;/bean&gt;
            &lt;/entry&gt;
        &lt;/map&gt;
    &lt;/constructor-arg&gt;
&lt;/bean&gt;
</code></pre>

