Q: Mongodb: find documents where at least one item in an array exists in an array field
A: <p>In case you are still keen on working the query with <code>$expr</code> operator,</p>
<ol>
<li><code>$ne</code> - Check the result from <em>1.1</em> not an empty array.</li>
</ol>
<p>1.1. <code>$setIntersection</code> - Intersect the <code>favorite</code> and input array to return an array with intersection.</p>
<pre><code>db.collection.aggregate([
  {
    $match: {
      $expr: {
        $ne: [
          {
            $setIntersection: [
              &quot;$favorites&quot;,
              [
                &quot;banana&quot;,
                &quot;orange&quot;
              ]
            ]
          },
          []
        ]
      }
    }
  }
])
