Q: How to write binary operator with two post operands syntax with Boost Spirit x3?
A: <p>Ok, here's the changes. The hard part is actually code-generating the builtin function.</p>

<h1>Parsing</h1>

<hr>

<h2>Step 1: extend AST</h2>

<p>Always start with the AST. We want operands that can be function calls:</p>

<p>In ast.hpp:</p>

<pre><code>struct function_call;  // ADDED LINE

// ...

struct operand :
    x3::variant&lt;
        nil
      , unsigned int
      , variable
      , x3::forward_ast&lt;unary&gt;
      , x3::forward_ast&lt;expression&gt;
      , x3::forward_ast&lt;function_call&gt; // ADDED LINE
    &gt;
{
    using base_type::base_type;
    using base_type::operator=;
};

// ...

enum funtoken
{
    fun_min,
    fun_max,
};

// ...

struct function_call : x3::position_tagged
{
    funtoken fun;
    std::list&lt;operand&gt; args;
};
</code></pre>

<p>In ast_adapted.hpp:</p>

<pre><code>BOOST_FUSION_ADAPT_STRUCT(client::ast::function_call,
    fun, args
