Q: PHP's mail() function messes up HTML in email message
A: <pre><code>$headers .= "...[snip]... boundary=\"----=MIME_BOUNDRY_message_parts\"\n"; 
                                    ^--here                          ^--here
</code></pre>

<p>You're embedding quotes into the boundary string, but not using the quotes for the actual boundaries.</p>

<p>The boundary portion on of the content-type header should not have quotes in it.</p>

<p>For multi-line string generation, particularly with embedded quotes (e.g. HTML), I <strong>STRONGLY</strong> suggest you use a HEREDOC:</p>

<pre><code>$message .= &lt;&lt;&lt;EOL
