<p>You already know that the string starts with <code>{</code> and ends with <code>}</code>, and doesn't have either of those two characters anywhere in the middle, so all you have to do is chop off the first and last characters. There's no reason to incur the cost of the temporary strings created by <code>TrimStart</code> and <code>TrimEnd</code>.</p>

