Q: How Microsoft planning to support Xamarin? Will we able to migrate existing Xamarin.iOS or Xamarin.Android project to MAUI?
A: <p>.NET MAUI is the successor to Xamarin.Forms specifically.</p>
<p>&quot;.NET for iOS&quot; is the successor to Xamarin.iOS and &quot;.NET for Android&quot; is the successor to Xamarin.Android.</p>
<p>If you are currently using a Xamarin.iOS or Xamarin.Android project (without Xamarin.Forms) you can migrate them to a new &quot;.NET for iOS&quot; or &quot;.NET for Android&quot; type project and keep most of the same code, with a few minor changes to your own codebase here and there (primarily namespace changes).</p>
<p>A very basic cproj file for a .NET for iOS project looks like this:</p>
<pre><code>&lt;Project Sdk=&quot;Microsoft.NET.Sdk&quot;&gt;
  &lt;PropertyGroup&gt;
    &lt;TargetFramework&gt;net8.0-ios&lt;/TargetFramework&gt;
    &lt;OutputType&gt;Exe&lt;/OutputType&gt;
  &lt;/PropertyGroup&gt;
&lt;/Project&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>(Using .NET 8 in this example, but 6, 7 or any higher version should work as well)</p>
<p>A few notes on migration of libraries and NuGet packages:</p>
<ul>
<li>Xamarin.Android libraries/packages can be used in a .NET For Android project. It's backwards compatible.</li>
<li>Xamarin.IOS libraries/packages can <strong>NOT</strong> be used in a .NET For iOS project. The creator of the library/package will have to update the package to support .NET for iOS (a lot of them have already done so)</li>
