<p>A possible way would be to return a code for the next step from the function if the path exists, otherwise 0 (although this might not be a recommended way for readable code, but just to propose the idea)</p>

<pre><code>int pathExists(char maze[][10], int sr, int sc, int er, int ec, int distance) {
    if (maze[sr][sc] != '.')
