Q: SipManager.newInstance returns null
A: <p>The Problem is that Android SDK is not supported over all the devices.<br>
you can check first whether it is supported on current device:  </p>

<pre><code> if(SipManager.isVoipSupported(getApplicationContext())){
     Log.d("VOIP:", "Supported!");
 }
 else{
     Log.d("VOIP:", "Not Supported");
 }
 if(SipManager.isApiSupported(getApplicationContext())){
     Log.d("API:", "Supported!");
 }
 else{
     Log.d("API:","NotSupported!");
 }
</code></pre>

<p>Sometime API is supported but not VOIP. I tested on <code>Moto E 2nd Gen.</code> and <code>Moto X 2014, 1st Gen.</code> Both API and VOIP is not supported on Moto X and Only API is supported on Moto E, but VOIP is not.<br>
To avoid this caveat, you can use 3rd party APIs such as <a href="http://www.doubango.org" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Doubango</a>.</p>

<p><strong>Source</strong>: <a href="http://obem.be/2014/06/04/sip-on-android.html" rel="nofollow noreferrer">SIP on Android</a>: This Article discusses this problem in detail and suggest alternative APIs.</p>

